WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.029
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:10.259
We have reached a lot of milestones lately.
For instance, we now have over one million

00:00:10.259 --> 00:00:16.090
views on the channel. In the next few days
we're also hoping to hit ten thousand subscribers.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:24.050
To put it in perspective, in 2015 August 20th,
we have had a 250 subscriber special episode

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:30.160
where my mind was pretty much blown. That
was only about 9 months ago. Whoa.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:35.300
For the record, here is an image that supposedly
contains ten thousand people. Just imagine

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:40.470
that they all have doctoral hats and you immediately
have a mental image of ten thousand of our

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:43.050
Fellow Scholars. It's insanity.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:47.940
And I must say that I am completely blown
away by your loyal support. Thanks so much

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:53.100
for everyone for the many kind messages, comments
and e-mails, of which I'll read quite a few

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:58.360
in a second. It just boggles the mind to see
that so many people are interested in learning

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:03.570
more about awesome new research inventions,
and I hope that it is as addictive to you

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:07.210
as it was for me when I first got to see some
of these results.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:12.649
A huge thank you also to our generous supporters
on Patreon, I find it really amazing that

00:01:12.649 --> 00:01:17.259
we have quite a few Fellow Scholars out there
who love the series so much that they are

00:01:17.259 --> 00:01:22.649
willing to financially help our cause. Just
think about it. Especially given that fact

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:27.539
that it's not easy to make ends meet these
days, I know this all too well being a full

00:01:27.539 --> 00:01:33.689
time researcher, doing Two Minute Papers and
having a baby is extremely taxing, but I love

00:01:33.689 --> 00:01:38.749
it. I really do. And I know there are people
who have it way worse, and here we have these

00:01:38.749 --> 00:01:43.560
Fellow Scholars who believe in this cause
and are willing to help out. Thanks so much

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.859
for each one of you, I am honored to have
loyal supporters like you.

00:01:47.859 --> 00:01:52.609
We are more than halfway there towards our
first milestone on Patreon, which means that

00:01:52.609 --> 00:01:58.119
our hardware and software costs can be completely
covered with your help. As you know, we have

00:01:58.119 --> 00:02:03.039
really cool perks for our Patrons. One of
these perks is that, for instance, our Professors

00:02:03.039 --> 00:02:07.840
can decide the order of the next episodes,
and I was really surprised to see that this

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:13.150
episode won by a record number of points.
Looks like you Fellow Scholars are really

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:16.540
yearning for some story time, so let's bring
it on!

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:22.830
The focus of Two Minute Papers has always
been what a work is about and why it is important.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:28.220
It has always been more about intuition than
specific details. That is the most important

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:34.350
reason why Two Minute Papers exists. But this
sounds a bit cryptic, so let me explain myself.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:39.910
Most materials on any scientific topic on
YouTube are about details. When this big deep

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:45.440
learning rage started, and it was quite fresh,
I wanted to find out what deep learning was.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:51.580
I haven't found a single video that was not
at least 30-90 minutes long, and all of them

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:56.770
talked about partial derivatives and the chain
rule, but never explained what we're exactly

00:02:56.770 --> 00:03:02.400
doing and why we are doing it. It took me
four days to get a good grasp, a good high-level

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.470
intuition of what is going on.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:09.780
I would have loved to have a resource that
explains this four days worth of research

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:16.680
work in just two minutes in a way that anyone
can understand. Anyone. I haven't found anything,

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:21.990
and this was just one example of many. Gandhi
said "Be the change that you wish to see in

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:29.650
the world", and this is how Two Minute Papers
was born. It has never been about the details, it has always been about intuition

